# Edison Computers — Full Code Review
## Project: Computer Repair Shop Management System
**Tech Stack:** C# · Windows Forms · Entity Framework Core · SQL Server · BCrypt · DI (Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection)
**Reviewed by:** Antigravity AI · March 2026

---

## 🏆 Overall Rating: 7.5 / 10

> **Summary:** This is a genuinely impressive first professional project. The architecture, design patterns, and code organisation are at a level most junior developers don't reach until their second or third serious project. Several areas show real professional thinking. There are also clear areas to grow, which is expected and healthy.

---

## Architecture & Design

### ✅ What You Did Right

| Area | Assessment |
|---|---|
| **3-Tier Layered Architecture** | Core → DAL → BLL → Presentation is clean and correct. Dependencies flow in one direction. |
| **Repository Pattern** | Generic `Repository<T>` base + specialised repositories (e.g. [JobRepository](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/DAL/Repositories/JobRepository/JobRepository.cs#16-540)) is the right approach. |
| **Dependency Injection** | Using `Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection` in a WinForms app is not common — this shows real initiative. Services are correctly scoped. |
| **Domain Model** | 12 domain models with proper relationships, navigation properties, and EF Core Fluent API config. |
| **ViewModels** | 20 ViewModels properly separate the UI concern from the domain model. |
| **Enums** | 12 strongly-typed enums instead of magic strings — excellent. |
| **Async/Await** | Correct use of async all the way through the stack. |
| **Password Hashing** | BCrypt is the correct choice. Used correctly for both hashing and verification. |
| **Migrations** | EF Core code-first migrations with `Database.Migrate()` on startup — professional practice. |
| **Soft Delete** | [RecordStatus](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/BLL/Services/CustomerService/CustomerService.cs#119-123) enum for customers and devices instead of hard-deletes — correct business decision. |
| **Decimal Precision** | `HasPrecision(18, 2)` configured correctly on all currency columns. |
| **Enum-to-String Storage** | Readable strings in the database instead of integers — smart for maintainability. |
| **Logging** | `LoggingService` used consistently across services — add, update, cancel, and error paths are all logged. |

