## Code Quality: Strengths

### Warranty Logic ([RepairRecord.cs](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/Core/Models/RepairRecord.cs))
The computed `WarrantyStartDate` and `WarrantyExpiryDate` properties with grace-period logic are **genuinely sophisticated** for a first project. The business logic (7-day grace period, start on collection date vs grace period end date, support for Days/Months units) is correctly encapsulated in the model itself as `[NotMapped]` properties. This is clean DDD-style thinking.

### Query Design ([JobRepository.cs](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/DAL/Repositories/JobRepository/JobRepository.cs))
- [GetJobDetailsForViewByIdAsync](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/DAL/Repositories/JobRepository/JobRepository.cs#217-265) uses a **single projected SQL query** with `.Select()` — this is an advanced EF Core pattern that avoids loading full entity graphs unnecessarily.
- [GetMonthlySummaryAsync](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/BLL/Services/DashboardService/DashboardService.cs#107-112) correctly splits work: fetch flat data from DB, then group in C# — good practical understanding of EF Core translation limits.
- Filtered `.Include()` (e.g. `j.RepairRecords.Where(...)`) for the billing query is excellent — only loads non-cancelled records.
- [GetTotalComponentChargeForJobAsync](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/DAL/Repositories/JobRepository/JobRepository.cs#350-369) does aggregation at the DB level with `SumAsync` — efficient.

### Validation ([CustomerService.cs](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/BLL/Services/CustomerService/CustomerService.cs))
- Duplicate check (phone + email) on both Add and Update (with exclusion of self on update) is correct.
- Custom [IsValidPhoneNumber](file:///d:/programming/EdisonComputersProject/EdisonComputers/BLL/Services/CustomerService/CustomerService.cs#219-231) with digit cleaning before validation is solid.
- `RegexOptions.Compiled` on the static email regex is a good performance micro-optimisation.

### Dashboard Service
- Modular dashboard with count methods, attention items, low-stock alerts, recent activities, and monthly summaries — covers real business needs well.

